{# What a request asks for beyond its scopes (RFC 9396 §2), in the language of the reader: one line per
   detail, said in the words of its own type under authorization_details.<type>, with the parameters that
   type chose to show. A type is a class the deployment wires, and the message it names is the one thing a
   user reads rather than recognises before agreeing to it. Included by the consent page of an interaction
   and by the page of the account that lists what is in force, so that a detail is said the same way
   wherever it is read. #}
{% trans_default_domain 'beffroi' %}
<ul data-authorization-details="{{ details|length }}">
    {% for detail in details %}
        <li data-authorization-detail="{{ detail.type }}">{{ ('authorization_details.' ~ detail.type)|trans(detail.rendering) }}</li>
    {% endfor %}
</ul>
